{"attachment": {"content": {"file": {"content": "# RAINBOW 3D — CLAUDE ACCOUNT TRANSFER AND SCREEN 05 MASTER PROMPT\n\n## Mission\nContinue my EXISTING playable Rainbow 3D Android game from GitHub. Do not start over, redesign approved screens, or substitute video/still images for real 3D gameplay. Aim for approximately 90–95% visual similarity to my approved reference images, verified by screenshots, while prioritizing efficient, high-impact changes.\n\n## Repository and recovery\nRepository: https://github.com/josiahscalia5-dev/rainbow-\nSource branch: `claude/rainbow-3d-account-transfer-syorak`\nHistorical branches to preserve: `ccr-e033f912-8b40f5`, `ccr-d4bb0ad3-8ycajb`, `claude/rainbow-3d-recovery-m4v347`, `ccr-6f431adf-7h0m8y`.\n\nFetch the source branch, verify its latest remote SHA, and create a safe new working branch from it if required. Compare any concurrent work before integrating. Never force-push or overwrite protected branches. Retrieve and verify Git LFS binaries, not pointer stubs. Recover all eleven reference screens, Benny and girl GLBs/animations, Blender files, Three.js/TypeScript/Android project, water/foam/coin/HUD assets, Google Flow integration, QA captures, scripts, specialist logs, and handoff documents. Report any missing items honestly.\n\n## Restore ten specialist agents\nRead `.claude/agents/` and restore saved configurations and unfinished tasks for: Reference Match Director; Benny Character Artist; Cartoon Girl Character Artist; Washer Environment Modeler; Water FX Specialist; Foam and Bubble Specialist; Path and Camera Transition Engineer; Animation and Gameplay Engineer; Playwright Visual QA Specialist; Android Build and Performance Specialist. Recreate agents from saved files rather than claiming running processes transfer between accounts. Assign nonoverlapping file ownership and resume from latest saved work.\n\n## CRITICAL NEW SCREEN 05 VISUAL BUILD METHOD\nApproved screen: **05 · FLOW INTO THE CURRENT**. Stop relying on endless tiny shader tweaks without whole-frame progress. First lock a reference-matched camera using vanishing point, ring positions, Benny placement, field of view, river width, and S-curve landmarks. Use Blender 5.3, the existing Screen 05 layout, and measured image-to-geometry alignment. All specialists must work against that camera lock.\n\nReconstruct the deep metallic violet/magenta perforated tunnel, reflective gold rings and small wall fittings, purple shadows, and a small warm distant light. Reject pale pink walls, giant orange loops, floating crossbars, and oversized glowing disks. Build a thick, glossy electric-cyan river with a genuinely winding S-shaped 3D path, flowing hot-pink bands, crests, troughs, cyan-white highlights, bubbles, and restrained foam banks. The far river must retain Screen 05's S-bends; do not show Screen 06's straight striped section prematurely. Use animated 3D geometry and shaders, not a static image.\n\nPreserve the latest corrected Benny model: round pink fluffy body, purple-and-white striped hat, pom-pom, gold star, and reference-matched proportions. Keep the fix removing white spikes/contact bands under Benny. Match coin trail positions, perspective, upright dollar signs, saturated gold faces, and milled rims. Prioritize overall composition, tunnel depth, and river geometry over minor coin polishing.\n\n## World Labs / Marble / Atlas evaluation\nInvestigate whether Blender-only reconstruction, Marble-assisted reconstruction, Atlas-assisted reconstruction, or a hybrid produces a faster, more accurate **small Screen 05 pilot**. Existing geometry and the cropped real-pixel reference may guide reconstruction. Check official tool availability, authentication, export format, import into Blender/Three.js, cost, and limitations. Marble website: https://marble.worldlabs.ai ; Atlas MCP endpoint to verify: https://api.atlas.worldlabs.ai/mcp ; official Marble skill repository to investigate: `worldlabsai/marble-developer-api-skill`. Do not assume installation equals authentication or that Claude subscription credits pay for World Labs. Ask before any separate paid external credits. Do not generate eleven worlds or repeatedly spend on failed pilots.\n\n## All screens and gameplay\nKeep all eleven screens and their order. Screen 04 retains the steep glowing blue five-arrow descent; Screen 05 is the primary visual pilot; Screen 07 descends deeply into Screen 08 Final Spin Chamber with no teleport/camera cut (previously measured about 61 game units). Preserve coin pickups, hearts, collision, pause/resume, movement, and ending. Recheck 05→06 and 07→08 continuity and Android performance. Keep Google Flow introduction/ending integration, with the girl never seeing Benny concealed in the purple towel; verify actual video files exist before claiming integration complete.\n\n## Tools and backups\nVerify GitHub, Blender/headless Python, Playwright, Android SDK/build tools, World Labs plugin/Atlas, Marble skill, and any existing Meshy/Rodin connectors. Report each as working/tested, needs authentication, missing, unsupported, or separately paid. Restore `.claude` settings, `CLAUDE.md`, session hooks, five-minute autosave, and health-check scripts. Test a real GitHub push and remote SHA equality. Never commit secrets. A container-local timer does not run while its cloud session is offline unless an independent scheduler is verified.\n\n## Proof and delivery\nFor a fixed Screen 05 gameplay checkpoint, produce separate full-resolution approved/current/new screenshots, a side-by-side, a 50% overlay, and a prioritized differences report. Compare geometry, camera, river shape, lighting, color, foam, Benny, and coins. Test nearby moving camera views, gameplay, regression screens, Android build, and steady-state draw calls. Do not claim 90–95% without convincing visual evidence. Preserve successful improvements and change approach when a full-frame iteration fails to improve.\n\n## Execute in this order\n1. Fetch and verify