h_statement`: the call is refused, changing nothing, if it does not match the target as it is when the user approves. Environments with unrestricted network access or a wildcard host are refused: start a new session on those instead. Network secrets saved on the target are sent to their hosts once this session has moved, and those saved on the current environment stop being used, which can take up to an hour; the approval prompt lists the hosts of both. If the user declines, or the call is refused, do not ask again in chat; carry on in this environment and say what remains blocked.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"properties": {"environment_id": {"description": "The target environment (env_...), exactly as passed to get_environment.", "type": "string"}, "mode": {"description": "Required. \"network_only\": the session's network follows the target environment and this machine is kept. No other value is accepted.", "enum": ["network_only"], "type": "string"}, "switch_statement": {"description": "The exact `switch_statement` get_environment returned for this environment_id: the target's name, the hosts it allows, package managers, MCP servers, its variable names and setup script with when each takes effect, and whose environment it is. Shown to the person approving; the call is refused if it does not match what the server computes after they approve.", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["environment_id", "switch_statement", "mode"], "type": "object"}, "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__switch_environment"}, "server": "claude-code-remote"}, {"description": "Unarchive a previously archived Claude Code Remote session. Transitions it back to active so it can accept events again; a fresh container will be provisioned on the next send_message. Use this to resume a session that was archived prematurely.", "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__unarchive_session", "schema": {"description": "Unarchive a previously archived Claude Code Remote session. Transitions it bac